  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"193\" data-end=\"409\">The <strong data-start=\"197\" data-end=\"263\">ALK-1 (Anaplastic Lymphoma Kinase 1) Rearrangement RT-PCR test</strong> detects genetic rearrangements or translocations involving the <strong data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"339\">ALK gene</strong> using <strong data-start=\"346\" data-end=\"406\">reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR)</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"411\" data-end=\"445\">This test is primarily used for:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"446\" data-end=\"768\">\n<li data-start=\"446\" data-end=\"579\">\n<p data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"579\"><strong data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"510\">Diagnosing ALK-positive non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC)</strong>, particularly <strong data-start=\"525\" data-end=\"544\">adenocarcinomas</strong> in younger, non-smoking patients</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"580\" data-end=\"661\">\n<p data-start=\"582\" data-end=\"661\">Detecting <strong data-start=\"592\" data-end=\"614\">ALK rearrangements</strong> in <strong data-start=\"618\" data-end=\"659\">anaplastic large cell lymphoma (ALCL)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"662\" data-end=\"768\">\n<p data-start=\"664\" data-end=\"768\">Rarely, it may be used in <strong data-start=\"690\" data-end=\"736\">inflammatory myofibroblastic tumors (IMTs)</strong> or other ALK-driven neoplasms</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"770\" data-end=\"941\">Identifying an ALK rearrangement is <strong data-start=\"806\" data-end=\"842\">critical for treatment decisions</strong>, as it predicts response to <strong data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"898\">ALK inhibitor therapies</strong> (e.g., crizotinib, alectinib, lorlatinib).</p>\n<p data-start=\"1001\" data-end=\"1139\">A <strong data-start=\"1003\" data-end=\"1022\">positive result</strong> indicates the presence of an ALK gene rearrangement, which is <strong data-start=\"1085\" data-end=\"1126\">clinically significant and actionable</strong>. It means:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1140\" data-end=\"1592\">\n<li data-start=\"1140\" data-end=\"1267\">\n<p data-start=\"1142\" data-end=\"1267\">The tumor is <strong data-start=\"1155\" data-end=\"1171\">ALK-positive</strong> and likely to respond to <strong data-start=\"1197\" data-end=\"1224\">targeted ALK inhibitors</strong>, which can dramatically improve outcomes</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1268\" data-end=\"1377\">\n<p data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1377\">In NSCLC, it helps guide first-line therapy away from conventional chemotherapy toward targeted treatment</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1378\" data-end=\"1506\">\n<p data-start=\"1380\" data-end=\"1506\">In ALCL, it supports diagnosis and may inform prognosis (ALK-positive ALCL typically has a better outcome than ALK-negative)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1507\" data-end=\"1592\">\n<p data-start=\"1509\" data-end=\"1592\">In IMTs, it confirms ALK-driven disease, which may also respond to ALK inhibitors</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1594\" data-end=\"1696\">A positive ALK test is a <strong data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1651\">strong therapeutic biomarker</strong> and often changes the entire treatment plan.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"1698\" data-end=\"1701\">\n<p data-start=\"1703\" data-end=\"1827\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">&nbsp;</p>",
